nightshades are a huge family of plants  many which we eat like potatoes tomatoes  peppers and eggplants some like  tomatillos and ground cherries have a  papery structure that grows around the  fruit it forms an air pocket that might  help the seeds disperse like a little  life raft this family comes from South  America where its fossil origins aren't  well known previously it was thought  that tomatillos and ground cherries  evolved fairly recently at the time the  Andes rose but new fossils that look  just like those wrapped up fruits were  recently described by researchers these  fossils prove that these plants were  around at a much earlier time than  anyone thought when South America was  still very close to hard to cut in  Australia and even southern South  America where the fossils were found was  warm and wet it also means these plants  evolved not just in South America but  likely in Antarctica too before it froze  over those are totally different  evolutionary conditions which makes you  wonder what else don't we know about our  favorite foods  [Music]
 

